---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const app = appBySlug('postscript')!;
const path = '/apps/postscript';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'apps/postscript');
const desc = description(site, 'apps/postscript');

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is Postscript still SMS only?",
    "answer": "No. Its Shopify listing markets SMS, RCS and email, with email rolling out in phases. The pricing page offers an email waitlist. Verify account access and required journeys before replacing an email sender."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should I estimate an 8,000-text month?",
    "answer": "Count billable segments, separate MMS and carrier fees, then add the selected base plan and optional services. Obtain a destination-specific estimate. The worked example below is illustrative, not a quote."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should I compare with Klaviyo SMS?",
    "answer": "Rehearse identical cart, purchaser suppression and sizing-reply cases. Compare event freshness, reply routing, number migration and full invoices. Neither platform is a universal winner."
  },
  {
    "question": "Do compliance features remove merchant responsibilities?",
    "answer": "No. Postscript advertises guardrails and support. Assign an owner for capture copy, permission records, imports and escalation. Test opt-out behavior and exclusions before enabling sends."
  },
  {
    "question": "Must I pair Postscript with Sequenzy?",
    "answer": "No. Retain an email sender that meets your needs, or evaluate Postscript email if available. Sequenzy is one possible email option. Choose from actual journey requirements and ownership."
  },
  {
    "question": "How does Recart differ?",
    "answer": "Recart emphasizes managed SMS and list growth. Postscript offers SMS tooling, AI products and a separate Postscript Plus managed-service add-on. Compare the service responsibilities you would purchase."
  },
  {
    "question": "How long does implementation take?",
    "answer": "There is no tested universal schedule here. Number provisioning, permission review, event validation and duplicate-flow shutdown determine readiness. Enable a bounded cohort after those checks pass."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should a reply rehearsal include?",
    "answer": "Ask for a specific size, an unavailable variant and an order change. Check approved product data, escalation and queue ownership. A marketing response must not promise an unauthorized order edit."
  },
  {
    "question": "Who should defer buying?",
    "answer": "Resolve missing permission evidence, unstaffed replies or an incomplete contribution model first. Monthly order count alone cannot establish whether SMS earns its cost."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/apps">All app reviews</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{app.name} review for Shopify stores</h1>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Current offering and review scope</h2>
      <p>Postscript offers Shopify-focused SMS capture, automations, segmentation and response management. Its current platform also advertises RCS and phased email access. This is a supplier-document review with proposed exercises, not a report of merchant trials or recovery results.</p>
      <p><a href="https://apps.shopify.com/postscript-sms-marketing">The Shopify listing</a> describes phased email rollout. <a href="https://postscript.io/pricing">Postscript’s pricing page</a> lists an email waitlist alongside SMS plans. Reviewed November 25, 2026. Ask which email journeys your account can use now before migrating authenticated sending, suppression records or post-purchase branches.</p>
      <p>RCS eligibility, device reach and fallback billing require an account-specific answer. Postscript Plus is a separate managed-marketing offering: product support, campaign strategy and shopper support are distinct jobs. Document which are included.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Shopify events and permission records</h2>
      <p>Create an event sheet with customer identity, phone, permission source and time, cart token, variant, order ID and arrival time. Follow a staff cart into the account. A Shopify order is purchase evidence, not by itself SMS marketing permission.</p>
      <p>Test a guest checkout that becomes a customer account, two phone formats for one buyer, and a purchase after a reminder is queued. Verify purchaser suppression and record the fallback if order events arrive late. Integration availability does not prove every field is synchronized.</p>
      <p>For subscriptions, distinguish add-on carts from renewals and failed-payment signals. Inspect actual fields from the subscription app. Blanket suppression of all subscribers can remove valid journeys; a stale tag can also allow an inappropriate one.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Number continuity and capture</h2>
      <p>Postscript lists a dedicated toll-free number among its marketing features. Before porting an existing number, record ownership, verification, provider release steps, expected interruption and rollback responsibility. Test inbound replies and opt-out after cutover, not only an outbound text.</p>
      <p>Rehearse a keyword and mobile popup with staff devices. Preserve displayed permission wording and the resulting record. Verify that email capture does not silently enroll SMS, repeat capture does not overwrite an opt-out, and the promised incentive matches the welcome message.</p>
      <p>An external popup tool is optional. If used, trace its record into Postscript, including field mapping and suppression updates. Assign someone to investigate rejected or contradictory records.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Pricing and sale-week sensitivity</h2>
      <p>The linked pricing page lists Starter with no base subscription and a $49 monthly minimum, Growth at $100 monthly and Professional at $500 monthly. Usage, carrier fees, optional products and destination differences remain material. Reconfirm the selected plan at purchase.</p>
      <p>Illustrative Growth arithmetic: 8,000 one-segment SMS at the displayed $0.008 rate cost $64. Using the displayed average US carrier fee of $0.00435 adds $34.80; with the $100 base, those lines total $198.80. This assumes the stated rate geography and excludes MMS, extra segments and add-ons. It is not a complete account quote.</p>
      <p>Build ordinary-month and drop-month estimates with actual copy, emojis and images. Recipient count alone cannot price multipart messages. Compare alternatives with the same destinations, message mix, number arrangement and service scope, without assuming a price winner.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Proposed exercise: limited sneaker cart</h2>
      <p>Use a $210 staff sneaker cart. Queue a no-discount reminder, then buy before the next touch. Repeat with the selected size sold out and a different variant available. These are proposed acceptance cases, not observed recovery outcomes.</p>
      <p>Inspect the phone deep link and its fallback. Do not assume the platform checks live stock before every send. If it cannot, remove claims that a scarce size is reserved or available and identify who pauses the flow during a stock-data outage.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Proposed exercise: VIP drop and offer control</h2>
      <p>Create a staff VIP cohort and an excluded recent purchaser. Compare source membership with the Postscript segment and inspect freshness before scheduling early access. Use a named timezone and verify account restrictions for recipient-local sending.</p>
      <p>Redeem the proposed shipping or percentage offer on eligible, excluded and sale items. Check stacking, expiry and an exhausted code. A tag import does not establish live synchronization with an external email sender.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Proposed exercise: sizing replies and order authority</h2>
      <p>Send “do you have 32x34?” during a simulated denim drop, then ask about an unavailable color. Inspect whether the answer uses current variant data and whether ambiguity reaches a named human queue. Check queue age and the history visible to the agent.</p>
      <p>Ask to change the size on an already placed order. Product recommendations do not confer order-edit permission. Define identity verification and transfer to authorized support before promising a stock hold, refund or shipment change.</p>
      <p>Approve product knowledge and offer rules before automated responses. Rehearse an ingredient question with a deliberately missing answer: acceptance requires escalation using approved guidance, not an invented health claim.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Proposed exercise: post-purchase review request</h2>
      <p>Create self-purchase, gift and partial-fulfillment cases. Inspect the delivery or fulfillment signal used for timing. An order-created timestamp does not establish that someone has received and used the product.</p>
      <p>Check for duplicate requests from another review app. Gift status may change recipient or wording; predicted satisfaction must not be used to solicit only favorable reviews. Assign ownership of the review destination and opt-out behavior.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Coordination and reversible launch</h2>
      <p>Inventory SMS automations, scheduled broadcasts and capture forms. Assign one sender per trigger. Pause the incumbent equivalent before enabling its replacement; preserve settings and identify an operator who can disable sends outside office hours.</p>
      <p>Choose email/SMS spacing from journey intent and tested account behavior. There is no universal three-hour minimum. Test a purchase between touches and an opt-out while a message is queued. Email opens alone are a weak basis for assuming a shopper missed a message.</p>
      <p>Enable only the accepted cohort, then review event exceptions and replies before widening it. Number, permission and queue failures determine the stop condition, not an arbitrary ninety-day trial or order threshold.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Contribution rather than attributed revenue</h2>
      <p>Deduplicate platform credits using Shopify order IDs. Record attribution windows, refunds, discounts, shipping subsidy and support labor. A dashboard credit does not prove the sale would disappear without SMS.</p>
      <p>Hypothetical experiment: split 1,000 eligible shoppers equally; 45 treated shoppers and 35 comparison shoppers purchase. With comparable assignment and observation, that is 10 additional orders among 500 treated shoppers. At $48 contribution each, the difference is $480 before incremental program cost. If that cost is $300, the example leaves $180.</p>
      <p>These are invented inputs for calculation, not Postscript results. Report uncertainty and check promotions and stock differences between groups. Do not extrapolate the difference to the entire store or call gross revenue profit.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Operating ownership before and after a drop</h2>
      <p>The campaign owner approves copy, offers and exclusions; support staffs the reply queue; the data owner checks event freshness; finance reviews projected usage. Record who can pause the campaign and how unresolved questions escalate.</p>
      <p>After sending, reconcile billed segments and carrier lines against the forecast. Inspect messages sent after purchase, opt-out exceptions and unresolved sizing questions. Expand only the specific workflows that justify their total cost.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card"><h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Related reading</h2><ul>
      <li><a class="link" href="/apps">apps</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-postscript">compare · klaviyo vs postscript</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">use cases · abandoned cart</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/apps/sequenzy">apps · sequenzy</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-postscript">compare · omnisend vs postscript</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/apps/recart">apps · recart</a></li>
      <li><a class="link" href="/apps/smsbump">apps · smsbump</a></li>
    </ul></div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Postscript Shopify FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
